{% doc %}
  The promises a RIFANO buyer needs before they press the button: cash on
  delivery plus delivery (one merged row), then warranty.

  One row each, icon plus a sentence at `--fs-sm` in `--c-text-2` with a hairline
  above and below the group. Never a coloured badge, never a stock counter,
  never a countdown: DESIGN.md's "trust" lever says the promise is never
  truncated or shrunk into micro-type, and that two mentions of it are already
  enough.

  Delivery and warranty come from theme settings (RIFANO → Livraison / Garantie /
  Retours); the COD line and the free-delivery half are the brand's standing
  commitments and are not editable per-product.

  @example
    {% render 'trust-badges' %}
{% enddoc %}

<ul class="trust">
  <li class="trust__row">
    {% render 'icon', name: 'cash', class: 'trust__icon' %}
    {%- comment -%}
      One row for the COD and delivery promise (it is already in the
      announcement bar, so a third mention is boilerplate). Keys are
      translated BEFORE being appended: `append | t` translates the whole
      joined string, which rendered as "Translation missing".
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign trust_text = 'rifano.trust_cod' | t -%}
    {%- if settings.delivery_text != blank -%}
      {%- assign trust_text = trust_text | append: ' · ' | append: settings.delivery_text -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign trust_free = 'rifano.trust_delivery_free' | t -%}
    {%- assign trust_text = trust_text | append: ' · ' | append: trust_free -%}
    <span class="trust__text">{{ trust_text }}</span>
  </li>

  {%- if settings.warranty_text != blank -%}
    <li class="trust__row">
      {% render 'icon', name: 'shield', class: 'trust__icon' %}
      <span class="trust__text">{{ settings.warranty_text }}</span>
    </li>
  {%- endif -%}
</ul>